This plugin adds the legacy ddclient backend to os-dyndns.  ddclient
is a Perl client used to update dynamic DNS entries for accounts on
many dynamic DNS services.

This plugin is deprecated and will be removed in a future release,
please use the native backend of os-dyndns instead.  To switch, select
the native backend in Services: Dynamic DNS: General settings and verify
your accounts are updated.  Then reinstall os-dyndns from the plugins
page so it is kept and remove os-ddclient.

Plugin Changelog
================

2.0

* Moved the dynamic DNS client and its native backend to os-dyndns
* Only provide the ddclient backend, which is used automatically
* Deprecated in favour of the os-dyndns native backend

Previous releases are listed in the os-dyndns changelog.
